IInnttrroodduuccttiioonn

This document describes how Postfix uses set-gid privilege elevation to gate
access from an unprivileged process to the Postfix queue and to core daemon
processes. It then presents an alternative privilege elevation mechanism for
systems that disable set-gid privilege elevation.

This guide assumes that Postfix uses the default settings: "mail_owner =
postfix" and "setgid_group = postdrop".

