    Postfix postlift Socket.

  * In case of problems, first look for Postfix logging (in /var/log/maillog or
    the like). If that does not reveal the problem cause, verify the socket
    status as shown above and look for failed service instances. These have
    names like postlift@xx-xx-xx.service. Examine each failed instance with a
    command like:

    # systemctl status postlift@xx-xx-xx.service

    and review the error logging at the bottom of the output.

